---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/landing.css";
import { url } from "../url.ts";

const i = (name: string) => url(`icons.svg#${name}`);
const shot = (name: string) => url(`screenshots/${name}.png`);
---
<Base title="Automatic Media Archive" description="AMA rips your CDs, DVDs and Blu-rays, works out what each one is, encodes it and puts it in your Plex Libraries.">
<main id="main" class="wrap">
  <section class="lead" aria-labelledby="hero-h">
    <div>
      <h1 id="hero-h">Put a Disc in, it turns up in Plex.</h1>
      <p class="lede">AMA rips your CDs, DVDs and Blu-rays, works out what each one is, encodes it and puts it in your Plex Libraries. It only asks you when it can’t tell.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn pri big" href="https://github.com/mintopia/automatic-media-archive/releases/latest"><svg class="i" aria-hidden="true"><use href={i("download")}/></svg>Download for Windows</a>
      <small>Windows 10 and 11 · free, MIT licence · <a class="guide" href={url("docs/install/")}>Read the install guide</a></small>
      <a class="btn big" href="#flow">See how a Disc flows</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="appwin hero-win" aria-labelledby="hero-cap">
    <div class="chrome"><svg class="i" aria-hidden="true"><use href={i("disc")}/></svg><b>AMA</b> in your browser · Now page<span class="tag">Example</span></div>
    <div class="inner"><picture>
      <source srcset={shot("now-mobile-dark")} media="(max-width: 720px) and (prefers-color-scheme: dark)" width="390" height="844">
      <source srcset={shot("now-mobile-light")} media="(max-width: 720px)" width="390" height="844">
      <source srcset={shot("now-desktop-dark")} media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
      <img src={shot("now-desktop-light")} alt="The Now page. Ocean’s Eleven is ripping at 49%, Firefly Disc 2 needs Review, Ocean’s Twelve is encoding, and History lists Ocean’s Thirteen, Firefly and Queen’s Greatest Hits." width="1440" height="850">
    </picture></div>
  </figure>
  <p class="wcap" id="hero-cap"><b>The app:</b> the Now page while Ocean’s Eleven rips. Ocean’s Twelve encodes alongside, and Firefly Disc 2 waits for you.</p>

  <section class="block" id="flow" aria-labelledby="flow-h">
    <h2 id="flow-h">How a Disc flows</h2>
    <p class="intro">The drive is the slow part, so AMA rips first and ejects at once. Everything else happens afterwards, from Scratch, a folder on the PC.</p>
    <ol class="stages">
      <li><h3>Ripping</h3><p>AMA copies the Disc to Scratch and ejects it, so the drive is free for the next one. CDs are checked against AccurateRip as they rip.</p><p class="you">You: put the next Disc in.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Review</h3><p>Only when it can’t tell: two films that fit the Disc equally well, a CD AccurateRip can’t verify, or which Titles are which Episodes.</p><p class="you">You: answer one question.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Encoding</h3><p>Films and TV are encoded to HEVC at the quality you set, on your graphics card if it can. CDs stay lossless FLAC.</p><p class="you">You: nothing.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Archived</h3><p>AMA names it with your Library’s Naming Pattern and moves it into the folder your Plex Library reads.</p><p class="you">You: press play.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <a class="more-link" href={url("docs/how-a-disc-flows/")}>Read the full walkthrough<svg class="i" aria-hidden="true"><use href={i("chevron")}/></svg></a>
  </section>

  <section class="block band" aria-labelledby="asks-h">
    <div class="asks">
      <div>
        <h2 id="asks-h" class="h2">It asks one question at a time</h2>
        <p class="intro">When AMA isn’t sure, it says so rather than guessing. It tells you on Discord, ntfy or your own Webhook:</p>
        <ul class="alerts">
          <li><svg class="i" aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--rev-ink)"><use href={i("alert")}/></svg><div><b>When a Disc needs you</b><span>DVD “FIREFLY_D2” needs Review before it can be archived.</span></div></li>
          <li><svg class="i" aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--arc-ink)"><use href={i("check")}/></svg><div><b>When a Rip is done</b><span>Blu-ray “OCEANS_ELEVEN” is ripped and ejected. Insert the next Disc.</span></div></li>
          <li><svg class="i" aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--fail)"><use href={i("eject")}/></svg><div><b>When a Job fails</b><span>What went wrong, and what to try next.</span></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <figure class="appwin" aria-labelledby="rev-cap">
          <div class="chrome"><svg class="i" aria-hidden="true"><use href={i("disc")}/></svg><b>AMA</b> in your browser · Review page<span class="tag">Example</span></div>
          <picture><source srcset={shot("review-tv-desktop-dark")} media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"><img src={shot("review-tv-desktop-light")} alt="Review for Firefly Disc 2: stills from each Title beside the Episode AMA suggests for it, S01E05 Safe to S01E08 Out of Gas." width="1440" height="850" loading="lazy"></picture>
        </figure>
        <p class="wcap" id="rev-cap"><b>The app:</b> AMA can’t tell which Title is which Episode, so it suggests an order and lets you check.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block gallery-block" aria-labelledby="look-h">
    <h2 id="look-h">Works at the drive and at the desk</h2>
    <p class="intro">Feed Discs with your phone in your hand, and do the odd Review on the big screen later.</p>
    <div class="gallery">
      <div><figure class="appwin" aria-labelledby="g1"><div class="chrome"><b>AMA</b> · Review page<span class="tag">Example</span></div><picture><source srcset={shot("review-film-desktop-dark")} media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"><img src={shot("review-film-desktop-light")} alt="Film Review for a Blu-ray labelled OCEANS: AMA’s best guess, Ocean’s Thirteen, beside stills from each Title and where it will be archived." width="1440" height="850" loading="lazy"></picture></figure><p class="wcap" id="g1"><b>Review</b>, confirming a film and its Main Feature from stills of each Title.</p></div>
      <div><figure class="appwin" aria-labelledby="g2"><div class="chrome"><b>AMA</b> · History page<span class="tag">Example</span></div><picture><source srcset={shot("history-desktop-dark")} media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"><img src={shot("history-desktop-light")} alt="History: Ocean’s Thirteen, four Episodes of Firefly and Queen’s Greatest Hits, newest first, each with where its details came from." width="1440" height="850" loading="lazy"></picture></figure><p class="wcap" id="g2"><b>History</b>, every Disc and what it became.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="fmt-h">
    <h2 id="fmt-h">What it handles</h2>
    <p class="intro">Video is kept as a good encode, not a full-size copy of the Disc. The Rip is deleted once the Encode is done.</p>
    <table class="handles">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Disc</th><th scope="col">What you get</th><th scope="col">Read with</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>CD</td><td><b>FLAC, lossless</b><small>Each Track is checked against AccurateRip; a Track that fails goes to Review.</small></td><td>cyanrip<small>AMA downloads it</small></td></tr>
        <tr><td>DVD</td><td><b>HEVC in MKV</b><small>Main Feature, Extras and Episodes, at the quality you set.</small></td><td>MakeMKV<small>you install it</small></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Blu-ray</td><td><b>HEVC in MKV</b><small>The same, from Blu-ray.</small></td><td>MakeMKV<small>you install it</small></td></tr>
        <tr><td>UHD</td><td><b>HEVC 10-bit with HDR10</b><small>HDR10 is kept. Dolby Vision and HDR10+ are not.</small></td><td>MakeMKV<small>you install it</small></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-h">
    <h2 id="install-h">Install</h2>
    <ol class="install">
      <li><b>Download the installer</b><p>AMA-Setup-x.y.z.exe from the latest GitHub release. It installs for your user only, so you don’t need admin rights.</p></li>
      <li><b>Run it, past the SmartScreen warning</b><p>The installer isn’t signed yet, so Windows warns you. Choose More info, then Run anyway.</p></li>
      <li><b>Finish Setup in your browser</b><p>AMA finds your drive, asks where your Libraries live and, if you have one, for a TMDB key. Then it’s ready for a Disc.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="reqs">You need <b>Windows 10 or 11</b> on the PC with <b>an optical drive</b>, and <b>Plex</b> somewhere that can see your Library folders. NVIDIA or Intel graphics make Encodes faster; any CPU works.</p>
    <div class="install-cta"><a class="btn pri big" href="https://github.com/mintopia/automatic-media-archive/releases/latest"><svg class="i" aria-hidden="true"><use href={i("download")}/></svg>Download for Windows</a><a class="btn big quiet" href={url("docs/install/")}>Read the install guide</a><small>For Discs you own.</small></div>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
